  "summary": "Web rendering is detached from database, native-auth, provider and job authority through fixed Core HTTP reads, an explicit command registry and preserved native protocol routes. A credential-free conventional Next production build and source/output graphs verify frontend import separation. An isolated production Next/Core/native PostgreSQL proof exercised authenticated SSR, a real thin Server Action cookie roundtrip, native auth relay, persisted commands, CSRF and cross-owner denials, metadata refresh and clean producer shutdown. Independent exact-diff source review covered the extraction and all final follow-ons without actionable findings.",
  "limitations": "Source and isolated local runtime qualification only. The original native proof at 7f9b9a927c4385ee0812b83f5d8a30ed2204ae45/package 1.7.2 is preserved. The follow-on native proof at ad41fbc4cba15ac35e178fb3facd8ea63100ea76/package 1.8.1 passed after Core admission and deployment-tooling corrections. It reused the production Web build from d1ecfa99e1dd93d35643fcffb312c9ce3e94590e, whose frontend runtime sources remain unchanged; that build used the preceding checkout as APP_COMMIT. The independent reviewer inspected source and evidence declarations without rerunning the application. The first hosted browser run passed public, mobile, shell and agency-project checks, then failed on deal-page reload; final-candidate hosted qualification remains required. An earlier bounded full-unit campaign did not finish. Full hosted application/PostgreSQL suites, Chromium qualification and all four CodeQL analyses remain separate required exact-main publication gates. No container/retained-installation, production deployment, Cloudflare adapter, provider delivery, tenancy, complete human journey or customer acceptance is claimed. The historical four-component custody path fails closed without separately qualified Core. Newsletter activation, subscriber intake and sending remain deferred.",
